---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const slug = 'ai-api-quick-reference-2026';
const date = '2026-08-11';
const locale = 'en';

const enTitle = 'AI API Quick Reference 2026: One-Page Documentation for All Major Providers';
const enDescription = 'Complete quick reference for 20+ AI APIs: endpoints, authentication, SDK examples, pricing, and migration guide. OpenAI, Anthropic, DeepSeek, Together AI, and more.';
const canonicalUrl = `https://apirank.vip/tutorials/${slug}`;
const zhCanonicalUrl = `https://apirank.vip/zh/tutorials/${slug}`;

const articleJsonLd = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "Article",
  "headline": enTitle,
  "description": enDescription,
  "datePublished": date,
  "dateModified": date,
  "author": {
    "@type": "Organization",
    "name": "APIRank",
    "url": "https://apirank.vip"
  },
  "publisher": {
    "@type": "Organization",
    "name": "APIRank",
    "logo": {
      "@type": "ImageObject",
      "url": "https://apirank.vip/favicon.svg"
    }
  },
  "mainEntityOfPage": {
    "@type": "WebPage",
    "@id": `https://apirank.vip/tutorials/${slug}`
  }
};

const breadcrumbJsonLd = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
  "itemListElement": [
    { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 1, "name": "Home", "item": "https://apirank.vip" },
    { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 2, "name": "Tutorials", "item": "https://apirank.vip/tutorials" },
    { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 3, "name": enTitle, "item": `https://apirank.vip/tutorials/${slug}` }
  ]
};

const faqJsonLd = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "FAQPage",
  "mainEntity": [
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Which AI API is cheapest for production use?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "For open-weight models, Together AI (Llama 4 at $0.20/M input), DeepSeek (V3 at $0.27/M), and FreeModel (aggregated pricing) are the cheapest. For closed models, xAI Grok-3 at $0.30/M is best value."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Do all APIs use the same authentication format?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Most use Bearer token in HTTP Authorization header (e.g., `Authorization: Bearer YOUR_API_KEY`), but some like Cloudflare Workers AI use API keys in headers. Check each provider's docs for exact format."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Can I switch between providers without changing my code?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Yes, if you use an aggregator like FreeModel, OpenRouter, or Block.AI. They normalize all provider APIs behind a single OpenAI-compatible endpoint, so you only change the base URL and API key."
      }
    }
  ]
};
---

<BaseLayout
  title={`${enTitle} | APIRank`}
  description={enDescription}
  canonicalUrl={canonicalUrl}
  zhCanonicalUrl={zhCanonicalUrl}
  articleJsonLd={articleJsonLd}
  breadcrumbJsonLd={breadcrumbJsonLd}
  faqJsonLd={faqJsonLd}
>
  <main class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-8">
    <div class="prose prose-gray max-w-none">
      <div set:html={`<h1>AI API Quick Reference 2026</h1>
<p><strong>Last updated:</strong> August 11, 2026<br />
<strong>Coverage:</strong> 20+ major AI providers with endpoints, authentication, code examples, and pricing</p>
<p>This is your one-stop reference for AI API integration in 2026. Whether you're building with OpenAI, Anthropic, DeepSeek, Together AI, or any of the other major providers, you'll find everything you need here.</p>
<hr />
<h2>📋 Table of Contents</h2>
<ol>
<li><a href="#openai">OpenAI</a></li>
<li><a href="#anthropic">Anthropic</a></li>
<li><a href="#deepseek">DeepSeek</a></li>
<li><a href="#together-ai">Together AI</a></li>
<li><a href="#xai-grok">xAI (Grok)</a></li>
<li><a href="#fireworks-ai">Fireworks AI</a></li>
<li><a href="#groq">Groq</a></li>
<li><a href="#hugging-face">Hugging Face</a></li>
<li><a href="#cerebras">Cerebras</a></li>
<li><a href="#sambanova">Sambanova</a></li>
<li><a href="#aggregators">Aggregators (FreeModel, OpenRouter, Block.AI)</a></li>
</ol>
<hr />
<h2>OpenAI</h2>
<p><strong>Best for:</strong> Production-grade models, best English performance, mature ecosystem</p>
<h3>Endpoint</h3>
<pre><code>https://api.openai.com/v1/chat/completions
</code></pre>
<h3>Authentication</h3>
<pre><code class="language-bash">Authorization: Bearer sk-xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
</code></pre>
<h3>Python SDK</h3>
<pre><code class="language-python">from openai import OpenAI

client = OpenAI(api_key=&quot;sk-xxxxx&quot;)

response = client.chat.completions.create(
  model=&quot;gpt-5.6&quot;,
  messages=[
    {&quot;role&quot;: &quot;system&quot;, &quot;content&quot;: &quot;You are a helpful assistant.&quot;},
    {&quot;role&quot;: &quot;user&quot;, &quot;content&quot;: &quot;Hello!&quot;}
  ]
)

print(response.choices[0].message.content)
</code></pre>
<h3>Pricing (per 1M tokens)</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>GPT-5.6:</strong> $2.50 input / $15.00 output</li>
<li><strong>GPT-5.5:</strong> $1.25 input / $7.50 output</li>
<li><strong>GPT-4o:</strong> $2.50 input / $10.00 output</li>
<li><strong>o1-pro:</strong> $15.00 input / $60.00 output</li>
</ul>
<h3>China Access</h3>
<p>❌ Not directly accessible from mainland China. Use aggregator (FreeModel/OpenRouter) or proxy.</p>
<hr />
<h2>Anthropic</h2>
<p><strong>Best for:</strong> Complex reasoning, long context (200K tokens), Claude Code integration</p>
<h3>Endpoint</h3>
<pre><code>https://api.anthropic.com/v1/messages
</code></pre>
<h3>Authentication</h3>
<pre><code class="language-bash">x-api-key: sk-ant-xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
Anthropic-Version: 2023-06-01
</code></pre>
<h3>Python SDK</h3>
<pre><code class="language-python">import anthropic

client = anthropic.Anthropic(api_key=&quot;sk-ant-xxxxx&quot;)

message = client.messages.create(
    model=&quot;claude-sonnet-5&quot;,
    max_tokens=1024,
    messages=[
        {&quot;role&quot;: &quot;user&quot;, &quot;content&quot;: &quot;Hello, Claude!&quot;}
    ]
)

print(message.content[0].text)
</code></pre>
<h3>Pricing (per 1M tokens)</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>Claude 3.7 Sonnet:</strong> $3.00 input / $15.00 output</li>
<li><strong>Claude 3.5 Sonnet:</strong> $3.00 input / $15.00 output</li>
<li><strong>Claude 3 Haiku:</strong> $0.25 input / $1.25 output</li>
</ul>
<h3>China Access</h3>
<p>❌ Not directly accessible. Use aggregator or proxy.</p>
<hr />
<h2>DeepSeek</h2>
<p><strong>Best for:</strong> China access, cheap production use, bilingual (EN/CN)</p>
<h3>Endpoint</h3>
<pre><code>https://api.deepseek.com/v1/chat/completions
</code></pre>
<h3>Authentication</h3>
<pre><code class="language-bash">Authorization: Bearer sk-xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
</code></pre>
<h3>Python SDK</h3>
<pre><code class="language-python">from openai import OpenAI

client = OpenAI(
    api_key=&quot;sk-xxxxx&quot;,
    base_url=&quot;https://api.deepseek.com/v1&quot;
)

response = client.chat.completions.create(
  model=&quot;deepseek-chat&quot;,
  messages=[
    {&quot;role&quot;: &quot;user&quot;, &quot;content&quot;: &quot;你好！&quot;}
  ]
)

print(response.choices[0].message.content)
</code></pre>
<h3>Pricing (per 1M tokens)</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>DeepSeek-V3:</strong> $0.27 input / $1.10 output</li>
<li><strong>DeepSeek-R1:</strong> $2.19 input / $8.75 output</li>
<li><strong>Free tier:</strong> $2 credit on signup</li>
</ul>
<h3>China Access</h3>
<p>✅ Fully accessible from mainland China. No VPN needed.</p>
<hr />
<h2>Together AI</h2>
<p><strong>Best for:</strong> Open-weight models (Llama 4, Qwen, Mistral), high throughput</p>
